Falsifies `page_frames::verification::an_allocated_frame_is_aligned_and_in_range`.

The defect: the bitmap index is added to the base without being scaled to an address, dropping
the `* FRAME_SIZE`. Index and address are both `u64`-shaped here and the expression type-checks
either way; at index zero the two agree, which is the case a first smoke test exercises.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(f.addr().is_multiple_of(FRAME_SIZE))`, for any index
other than zero, where `alloc` returns an address inside the first frame of the region rather
than the frame it reserved the bit for.

diff --git a/crates/page_frames/src/lib.rs b/crates/page_frames/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/page_frames/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/page_frames/src/lib.rs
@@ -260,3 +260,3 @@
         self.hint = i + 1;
-        Some(PageFrame(self.base + i as u64 * FRAME_SIZE))
+        Some(PageFrame(self.base + i as u64))
     }
